<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wolf Dietrich von Raitenau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1559">1559</a>–<a href="/years/1617">1617</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wolf Dietrich von Raitenau was Prince-Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> from 1587 to 1612. He began rebuilding the city in Italian baroque style, clearing space for a new cathedral and building the Mirabell palace for his companion Salome Alt, but after a conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> over salt he was deposed and died imprisoned in the fortress of Hohensalzburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wolf-dietrich-von-raitenau.jpg" alt="Wolf Dietrich von Raitenau" width="320" height="343" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Caspar Memberger the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wolf-Dietrich_von_Raitenau_P1380516.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
